## Why Hooks Might Not Appear

### Issue 1: No Git Repository
```bash
# Hook checks this and exits silently:
git diff HEAD~1..HEAD --name-only 2>/dev/null

# If no git repo → returns nothing → hook exits
```

**Solution**: Initialize git
```bash
cd ~/your-project
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial setup"
```

---

### Issue 2: No Recent Commit
```bash
# Hook needs HEAD~1 (previous commit)
CHANGED_FILES=$(git diff HEAD~1..HEAD --name-only)

# If only one commit exists → HEAD~1 doesn't exist → no output
```

**Solution**: Make at least 2 commits
```bash
git commit -m "First commit"
# Make changes
git add .
git commit -m "Second commit"  # Now hooks work
```

---

### Issue 3: Wrong File Type
```bash
# API standards hook only checks REST annotations
if ! echo "$DIFF_CONTENT" | grep -qE "@RestController"; then
    exit 0  # Exits silently if no REST API
fi
```

**Triggers on**: Java files with `@RestController`, `@GetMapping`, etc.

**Doesn't trigger on**: Plain Java classes without REST annotations

---

### Issue 4: Hook Output Not Visible in Conversation

**In normal Claude Code CLI**:
- Hooks run automatically
- Output displays in your terminal
- You see status messages and results

**In this conversation**:
- Hooks run but output isn't captured in tool results
- Hook output goes to Claude Code interface (not chat)
- You can manually run hooks to see output:

```bash
cd ~/your-project
bash ~/team-claude-config/hooks/post-code/api-standards-check.sh
```

