## Testing Hooks Manually

### Test Complexity Hook
```bash
export CLAUDE_USER_PROMPT="implement authentication system"
bash ~/team-claude-config/hooks/pre-user-prompt/task-complexity-check.sh
```

Expected output:
```
🔍 Pre-flight task complexity assessment...

Estimated Complexity Score: 3

⚡ MODERATE COMPLEXITY
```

---

### Test Code Quality Hooks

**Setup**:
```bash
cd ~/test-project
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial"

# Make a change to a Java file
echo "class Test {}" > TestController.java
git add .
git commit -m "Add controller"
```

**Run hooks**:
```bash
# SOLID check
bash ~/team-claude-config/hooks/post-code/solid-check.sh

# Domain review
bash ~/team-claude-config/hooks/post-code/domain-review.sh

# API standards
bash ~/team-claude-config/hooks/post-code/api-standards-check.sh
```

---

### Test Pre-Commit Hooks

**Setup**:
```bash
cd ~/test-project
echo "changes" >> file.txt
git add .
# Don't commit yet
```

**Run hooks** (simulates post-commit):
```bash
bash ~/team-claude-config/hooks/pre-commit/security-check.sh
bash ~/team-claude-config/hooks/pre-commit/test-coverage.sh
```

